[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-INTRODUCTION
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-INTRO-PURPOSE
STATEMENT: >>>
These Member High Level Requirements refine Member Frontend Platform Integration Requirements into Member Frontend functionality. This document is a rough draft for v5.0.1 Member Frontend scope. REVIEW_STATUS values are Changed, not Baselined, except where a Wave ticket Approves the HLR slice it refines. Broad HLR refinement continues under GSSC5-78; Wave tickets may refine in-scope shell HLRs in the same PR (for example Header under GSSC5-81 and Footer under GSSC5-82).
<<<

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-INTRO-SCOPE
STATEMENT: >>>
In-scope for this rough draft: authentication and session guards; application shell (root, header, footer, generic sections, generic editor, contact-row primitives); dashboard; content editors for public pages and sections, announcements, events, newsletters, and publications/tools; account self-service and administrator account management; members directory and search.
<<<

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-INTRO-ELECTIONS-OUT
STATEMENT: >>>
Out of v5.0.1 for this draft: elections (GSSC-PIR-13). Do not treat election HLRs as in-scope for v5.0.1. GSSC-PIR-13 remains an Approved PIR for a later release; this document does not invent election HLRs.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-APPLICATION
TITLE: Application Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-MEMBER-FRONTEND
TITLE: Member Frontend

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-1
TITLE: Member Frontend Application
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website SHALL have a members-only frontend application.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This is the Member Frontend. The other Member requirements describe that application. The Public Frontend is a separate application.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-21
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-2
TITLE: Members-Only Subdomain
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL be served on the members-only subdomain.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Member Frontend is the application on the members-only subdomain. This requirement does not set the subdomain name. The Public Frontend is on the public-facing primary domain.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-21
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-AUTHENTICATION
TITLE: Authentication Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-LOGIN
TITLE: Login

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-3
TITLE: Login Required
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL require a member to log in before accessing Member Frontend contents other than the login experience.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members-only contents are available only after login. The login experience itself remains reachable without a prior login so a member can authenticate.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-32
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-4
TITLE: Login Credentials
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL accept a member's username or primary email, together with that member's password, for login.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names the credentials a member enters. Login requires an account identity the Unified Backend already accepts (username or primary email) plus a password. Credential verification is performed by the Unified Backend.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-86
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-5
TITLE: Login Success
STATEMENT: >>>
When login succeeds, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL treat the member as logged in for subsequent Member Frontend access.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful login has to establish a usable Member Frontend session. The Unified Backend issues and retains the Login Token; the Member Frontend consumes that session rather than minting its own token.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-6
TITLE: Login Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
When login fails, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL leave the visitor logged out and show that login did not succeed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A failed login must not grant Member Frontend contents. Feedback tells the visitor that authentication did not succeed without exposing Unified Backend internals.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-SESSION
TITLE: Session

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-7
TITLE: Session Challenge
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL determine whether a visitor is logged in by challenging the Unified Backend Login Token session.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a session challenge. The Member Frontend relies on the Unified Backend Login Token cookie and challenge rather than storing a raw login token itself.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-8
TITLE: Invalid Session
STATEMENT: >>>
When the Login Token session is invalid or absent, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL treat the visitor as logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An invalid or missing session must not grant Member Frontend contents. The visitor is treated as logged out until a later login succeeds.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-9
TITLE: Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-in member chooses logout, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL end that member's Login Token session, leave the visitor logged out, and take that visitor to the login experience without preserving the page they left as a return destination.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires logout. A logged-in member needs a way to end the session. Logout ends the Unified Backend Login Token session for that member. Explicit logout should land on login as a clean start rather than bouncing the member back to the page they just left.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
GSSC5-87
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-GUARDS
TITLE: Guards and Redirects

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-10
TITLE: Unauthenticated Redirect
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-out visitor requests Member Frontend contents other than the login experience, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL redirect that visitor to the login experience and include the attempted Member Frontend destination in the login query so a later successful login can return there.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login is required before contents. A logged-out visitor who requests protected contents is sent to login rather than shown those contents. Carrying the attempted destination in the query preserves deep links across authentication, except when logout intentionally omits a return destination.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-88
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-32
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-11
TITLE: Post-Login Destination
STATEMENT: >>>
When login succeeds after an unauthenticated redirect, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL take the member to the Member Frontend destination that member originally requested when that destination is still available, otherwise to the dashboard.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a post-login destination. Returning the member to the requested destination avoids forcing a detour through the dashboard when a deep link was the reason for login. The dashboard is the fallback home page.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-12
TITLE: Authenticated Login Redirect
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-in member requests the login experience, the GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL redirect that member away from the login experience to the return destination in the login query when that destination is still available, otherwise to the dashboard.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member who is already logged in does not need the login experience. Honoring a return destination in the query keeps deep-link behavior consistent with post-login redirects; the dashboard remains the Member Frontend home page fallback.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-88
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-SHELL
TITLE: Application Shell Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ROOT
TITLE: Root

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-13
TITLE: Application Root
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a root layout that hosts the Header, the active Member Frontend view, and the Footer for authenticated contents.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a root layout. Authenticated Member Frontend views share a common shell so header and footer placement stay consistent across pages.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-14
TITLE: Common Page Errors
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, a Member Frontend view SHALL display error contents when an error occurs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR allocates how a view presents an error. A Member Frontend view displays the error contents so the member sees the error that occurred.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-HEADER
TITLE: Header

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-15
TITLE: Header Presence
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, an authenticated Member Frontend view SHALL include the Header at the top of the view.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR allocates placement of the Header. This is the default placement of the Header on authenticated Member Frontend views.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-16
TITLE: Header Logo
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL include the GSSC Logo.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a logo. The Public Frontend Header includes the GSSC Logo. The Member Frontend Header keeps that brand signal for logged-in members.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-17
TITLE: Header Greeting
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL greet the logged-in member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a greeting. The Header shows the logged-in member that the Member Frontend recognizes them.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-18
TITLE: Header Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL offer logout to the logged-in member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout ends the member's session. Placing logout in the Header keeps that control available from authenticated views.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-19
TITLE: Header Navigation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL provide navigation to the dashboard and to the Member Frontend areas the logged-in member is permitted to open.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires header navigation. Logged-in members need a consistent way to reach the dashboard and other Member Frontend areas their permissions allow. This is Member Frontend area navigation, not a clone of the Public Frontend Header action bar.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-81
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-60
TITLE: Header Login
STATEMENT: >>>
When no member is logged in, the GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL offer login.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR places login in the Header. A logged-out visitor on the Member Frontend needs a Header path to the login experience. The login experience contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-FOOTER
TITLE: Footer

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-20
TITLE: Footer Presence
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless otherwise specified, an authenticated Member Frontend view SHALL include the Footer at the bottom of the view.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR allocates placement of the Footer. This is the default placement of the Footer on authenticated Member Frontend views.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-82
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-21
TITLE: Footer Organization Name
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL include the full name of the Genealogical Society of Stanislaus County from the website's society contact data, without substituting the society acronym for that full name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires the organization's name in the Footer. The Public Frontend Footer includes the society's full name from shared society contact data. The Member Frontend Footer keeps that full name in every layout and does not replace it with the acronym.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-82
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-22
TITLE: Footer Copyright
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL include a copyright statement for the Genealogical Society of Stanislaus County.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a copyright statement. The Public Frontend Footer includes a copyright statement. The Member Frontend Footer keeps a copyright statement for the society and does not set its exact wording.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-82
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-70
TITLE: Footer Phone Number
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL include the society's phone number.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires the society's phone number. The Public Frontend Footer includes that phone number. The Member Frontend Footer keeps the phone number separate from the Contact overlay and does not set the current number.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-82
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-71
TITLE: Footer Email Address
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL include the society's email address.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires the society's email address. The Public Frontend Footer includes that email address. The Member Frontend Footer keeps the email address separate from the Contact overlay and does not set the current address.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-82
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-72
TITLE: Footer Postal Address
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL include the society's postal address.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires the society's postal address. The Public Frontend Footer includes that postal address. The Member Frontend Footer keeps the postal address separate from the Contact overlay and does not set the current address.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-82
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-73
TITLE: Footer Contact
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Footer SHALL offer a Contact control that opens a contact overlay for drafting a message to the organization.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR requires a footer contact option. The Public Frontend Footer opens a contact overlay. The Member Frontend Footer keeps that path; overlay contents may land in a later ticket.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-82
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-GENERIC-PRIMITIVES
TITLE: Generic Primitives

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-23
TITLE: Generic Section Display
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a generic section display that places a section's contents for a logged-in member through a shared Section Container, including optional header, featured image, body, and resources.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names a generic section display. Page and content editing reuse a shared section presentation so members see section contents consistently without programming knowledge.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-83
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-24
TITLE: Generic Editor
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a generic editor that lets a member with the necessary permissions modify editable contents without programming knowledge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Member content and public-page editing PIRs require modification without programming knowledge. A shared generic editor is the Member Frontend capability those editors reuse. Field-level editing rules are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-84
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-25
TITLE: Contact Row Primitive
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide a contact-row primitive that presents a person's name and the contact methods made available for that person.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names a contact-row primitive. Account views and the members directory reuse a shared contact presentation for names and contact methods.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-85
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-61
TITLE: Form Field Primitives
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL provide shared form-field primitives for labeled text entry, labeled selection, a zip-and-extension row, and a password-criteria list that member forms reuse without reimplementing field chrome.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names form-field primitives. Account forms, directory search, and editors need consistent field chrome (floating labels, required markers, zip-plus-extension, password criteria icons).
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-85
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-DASHBOARD
TITLE: Dashboard Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-26
TITLE: Dashboard Home Page
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL use the dashboard as its home page for a logged-in member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Member Frontend home page is the dashboard after login.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-56
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-27
TITLE: Dashboard Contents
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL present the dashboard contents provided for the logged-in member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The dashboard is the Member Frontend home page. Its modifiable contents come from the Unified Backend. This requirement presents those contents and does not set their structure.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-56
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-28
TITLE: Dashboard Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a member with the necessary permissions modify the dashboard contents without programming knowledge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR separately requires dashboard editing. Authorized members need to keep dashboard contents current without developer intervention, consistent with other Member Frontend content editing.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: Account Requirements

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-OWN-ACCOUNT
TITLE: Own Account

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-29
TITLE: Own Account Access
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member open that member's own account on an Account Page that presents Member Information, Account Information, and Password Change sections.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members manage their own accounts from the Member Frontend. The shared three-section Account Page is the self-service surface.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-30
TITLE: Own Account View
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member view that member's own account information in the Member Information and Account Information sections of the Account Page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member can see the account information held for that member. Section layout and field sets are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-31
TITLE: Own Account Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member modify the Member Information and Account Information that member is permitted to change, including name, contact, addresses, account photo, and username, and SHALL gray membership status and position when that member is not a user moderator.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Self-service account management includes changing permitted fields. Membership status and position stay read-only for ordinary members. Permission switches belong to administrator account management.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-32
TITLE: Own Password Change
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member change that member's own password from the Password Change section, with live criteria that report matching confirmation, minimum length, lowercase, uppercase, number, and special character.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names password change. Own-account management includes replacing the password used for login. Live criteria guide a valid replacement. Password recovery flows that do not require a logged-in Member Frontend session are outside this requirement.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-33
TITLE: Own Directory Contact Visibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a logged-in member choose which of that member's contact methods are available to fellow members in the members directory.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The members directory shows contact information members make available. Own-account management is where a member controls that availability.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-90
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-10
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-12
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-ADMIN-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: Administrator Account Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-34
TITLE: Administrator Account Management Access
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator open a selected member's Account Page that presents the same Member Information, Account Information, and Password Change sections used for own-account management.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderators manage member accounts from the Member Frontend. An administrator is a user moderator. Sharing the Account Page layout keeps self-service and management visually consistent.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-35
TITLE: Administrator Account View
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator view a selected member's account information in the Member Information and Account Information sections.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderators need to inspect member accounts. An administrator is a user moderator. Which fields appear is low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-36
TITLE: Administrator Account Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let a user moderator modify a selected member's Member Information and Account Information that moderator is permitted to change, including editable membership status and position, and SHALL let an administrator set every site privilege with switches while a non-administrator viewer sees only the selected member's active privileges as a list.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
User moderator account management includes changing permitted fields on another member's account. Privilege switches are administrator-only. An administrator is a user moderator for membership status and position.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-11
GSSC5-91
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MHLR-37
TITLE: Administrator Account Creation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend SHALL let an authorized administrator create a member account.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Member Frontend PIR names account creation. Administrator account management includes adding a registered member so that member can later log in.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-11
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed

